  "ref": "2KI.17.37",
  "review_notes": [
    "The flagged three-morpheme unit כָּל־הַיָּמִים → *for evermore* was not indivisible as it stood. Rule 30 allows the two lexical morphemes to share the one English rendering but states in the same breath that the fusion never absorbs a morpheme whose sense the rendering does not carry, and gives the parallel of דִּבְרֵי הַיָּמִים → *chronicles*, where the separately segmented article takes a written *the* or is its own unrepresented unit. No *the* is written here.",
    "The supplied *for* stays inside that unit as the adverbial accusative's own function word (rule 33), and the head remains on יָמִים."
  ]
